# The selected coefficient prime is nonzero

Theorem statement: `MTT.Eigenform.coefficientPrime_ne_bot` (`31da2baf-82a1-4404-8629-e3e2e6849f39`),
by davidloeffler, 2026-09-20.

Proof: submission `2b2643b3-b2db-4e19-9694-c01e84aa95a1`, by davidloeffler, 2026-09-20 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

The prime ideal of the eigenform coefficient field selected by a
$p$-adic embedding is not the zero ideal. Indeed, it contains the nonzero
rational integer $p$.

## Explanation of the source proof

The preceding theorem puts the rational integer `p` in the coefficient prime. If the ideal were
bottom, this would make `p` zero in the integer ring, contradicting primality of `p`. The uploaded
theorem is at `_root_.solution`.

